{
 "id": "2026-11-22-cop31-ends-without-deal",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Nearly two hundred countries. Two weeks of talks. No climate deal. What broke it?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "COP thirty-one in Antalya, Türkiye, ended Sunday with no deal. President Murat Kurum said there was no agreement on the text. Al Jazeera reports it is the first time since Copenhagen in 2009 that U.N. climate talks ended this way."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "The fault line was fossil fuels. CNN reports the first draft called for a transition away from them, but later drafts dropped every mention, despite a push by more than one hundred countries. The European Union and Panama refused to back a deal without it."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Developing countries also said it lacked new money to adapt. A one hundred twenty billion dollar target had been dropped. U.N. chief António Guterres said he was deeply disappointed. Open issues move to COP thirty-two, in Ethiopia, next year."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will COP thirty-two in Ethiopia agree on fossil fuels? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
