 "upload": {
  "title": "COP31 Collapses With No Climate Deal #shorts",
  "description": "The UN climate summit COP31 in Antalya, Türkiye, ended on Sunday without an agreed outcome. COP31 President Murat Kurum said there was no agreement on the text, so it was not adopted; Al Jazeera reports it is the first time since Copenhagen in 2009 that UN climate talks failed to end with a deal adopted by all. According to CNN, the first draft called for a transition away from fossil fuels, but every later draft dropped the words despite a push by more than 100 countries; the European Union and Panama refused to back a deal without it. Developing countries also objected that the text lacked new adaptation money after a $120 billion target was dropped. UN Secretary-General António Guterres said he was \"deeply disappointed\". Unresolved issues move to COP32 in Ethiopia in 2027.\n\nSources: Al Jazeera, CNN, NBC News, CBS News, Euronews, NPR, UN News, CBC News (based on search-result excerpts). Map locations are for orientation.\n\n#climate #cop31 #fossilfuels #climatechange #antalya",
